<<~ ahu slot=`#/r3-yin-roadmap-placement`>>

!!! Roadmap placement


''MEASURED (confirmed-by-both):'' K15 owns one identity, store, registry, archive and content-key seat per PersonaGroup; K15 step 6 migrates identity bytes, split stores and archive format together (`stable-founding-road.mem:203,456`; `keyhive-per-persona-group-2026.mem:55-72`). F6 slice three consumes face context for asker-sealed writes (`stable-founding-road.mem:504`). ''LEAD (confirmed-by-both):'' define the exhaustive D/F/S row schema, independent FCK and slot/recovery tree in K15.1; establish per-face ownership and remove above-face identity delegation in K15.1/.2; bind each tab to one face/session and apply (a′) in K15.3 + F6 slice three, ensuring the selected sealer can open the existing row before replacement; complete face-only removal in K15.4 and one-face recovery/restore in K15.5; move identity bytes, split stores, FCK slots and archives behind one migration fence in K15.6. F6 routes writes over this established key ownership; it cannot grant isolation over a VK. Build floor rows without a vessel key throughout, and make node-only VK contingent on a measured S row. Sources: `../PRIOR-YIN.md:66-89`, `../PRIOR-YANG.md:56-69`, `sealed-writer.ts:208-218,279-309`.

