<<~ ahu slot=`#/r4-yin-1-ratchet-twin-claims-against-source`>>

!!! 1. Ratchet: TWIN claims against source


| TWIN claim | Verdict after opening cited source | Provenance |
| Node founds VK, SK, and custody root; VK opens SK through serving tree. | ''CONFIRM.'' `packages/lararium-node/src/custody-session.ts:80-116,154-190,227-242` mints VK/SK, writes SK tree under VK and opens both on unlock. | twin-alone |
| No serving carrier exists yet; Herm does not presently consume SK to raise/read. | ''CONFIRM.'' `vault-carriers.ts:12-14,249-251` says no serving row stands. `vessel-standing.ts:60-79,113-119` fixes Herm persona ceiling at zero and says raised operator caps ride with the recognized operator. `open-node-vessel.ts:3242-3291` composes Herm; the cited raise path is separate. This makes SK a future conditional secret, not today's Herm S row. | twin-alone |
| Herm has no seated PersonaGroup (`personaSlotCeiling("herm") === 0`). | ''CONFIRM.'' The implementation returns zero unconditionally for Herm. | twin-alone |
| Node's place signing seed is private and currently floor-loaded, and is distinct from VK/SK. | ''CONFIRM, with consequential qualification.'' `node-vessel-identity.ts:429-442` reads private `signingKey` from a local key file; `:451-487,491-499` separates floor signing/device capability from PersonaGroup root. `vault-carriers.ts:239-251` explicitly puts `vessel-key` and `sk-slots` at floor; `open-node-vessel.ts:3283` supplies seed to Herm. It is confidential, auto-loaded at boot, and not VK or SK. However, it is a private vessel key at floor by the source's own naming. That ''breaks'' an unqualified “floor holds no vessel key / floor contains only public material” law. TWIN's proposed exception is not the operator's existing ruling; it needs an explicit house ruling or a code/design change. | twin-alone |
| Node's current VK/SK hierarchy is not a reason to keep face rows under VK. | ''CONFIRM.'' Current carrier table `vault-carriers.ts:287-398` describes placement. The prior-round census independently sorts private face-bearing pieces D and public artifacts F; it found no necessary browser S. | confirmed-by-both |
| Container restart cannot itself authorize private work. | ''CONFIRM as target, not an observed orchestrator policy.'' Roadmap says every boot starts at floor and a sovereign verb refuses pending `lares vault unlock` (`stable-founding-road.mem:66-68`); container entry point is `tools/lares-container.sh` named at `:68`; `founding-runbook.mem:156` covers unlock flow. No source here establishes unattended orchestrator credential delivery, so no claim that every deployed orchestrator behaves safely. | twin-alone |
| CLI and MCP do not each hold separate vessel secrets; face authority must be presented at the node gate. | ''CONFIRM as roadmap target.'' `stable-founding-road.mem:201` says CLI/MCP run proves face; `packages/lares-cli/src/sealed-act-door.ts:1-21`, `custody-door.ts:2-26`, `custody-frames.ts:135-202` implement the seat/door framing. | twin-alone |
| Guest island is an established separate key store / vessel. | ''REFUTE as measured.'' `device-capabilities-2026.mem:142-143` identifies Mudlet as a probe/leaf behind a node and Unreal as guest island/camera-on-streaming-server, but `wiki-layer-ontology.mem:249` defines a Lua object-model guest, not an independent custody store. Separate guest-owned keys would make it a new vessel by LEAD; source does not prove they exist. | twin-alone |
| Mobile/browser worker lifetime can hold custody across suspension. | ''REFUTE as authority claim.'' House matrix reports iOS no SharedWorker lifetime guarantee and Android support varies by version (`device-capabilities-2026.mem:137-140`). Safari's official extension guidance requires iOS nonpersistent background pages and says use storage to save/restore state ([[Apple Developer|https://developer.apple.com/documentation/safariservices/optimizing-your-web-extension-for-safari?changes=_5]], accessed 2026-10-19). Worker liveness cannot substitute for each tab/session's face admission. | confirmed-by-both |

