!!! 3. Every vessel type and one red test each


Rows refer to the common act census in `../PRIOR-YIN.md` (“Census of current vessel-common carriers and acts”) and `../PRIOR-YANG.md` (“Census — each currently vessel-common row act”), read 2026-10-19. In short: founding and slot trees; join offer/request/answer/land/pending; face slot changes and rotation; roster/labels/declarations; Keyhive/Veil archives; handle/circle routing; dyads/face proof/member/Nexus keys; transport configuration; recovery/bundle/restore; clear-custody. Their private face pieces are D; signed offers/public cards, charters, pins, public config and minimum deliberate route bytes are F. Mixed existing carriers must be split. Current browser one-VK tree: `packages/lararium-browser/src/browser-custody.ts:2-12,54-68,386-402`; current node classes: `packages/lararium-node/src/vault-carriers.ts:239-398`.

| Type / current common rows → target | S set and interaction | Face unlock / floor or shutdown transition | Bend / house ruling | Single red test |
| ''LarVessel class / worker host'' (`lar-vessel.mem:20-24,34-40`) | D per face, F public/bootstrap; no additional S absent named payload. | Owning face opens its own FCK; last face session discards it. | Host capability is not authority. | Give worker A context, bypass router and open/replace B ciphertext: refuse; A own-row replacement passes. |
| ''Desktop browser, laptop leaf'' (`device-capabilities-2026.mem:133,140`) | Census D/F; S=∅. Person enters that face's passphrase/paper route or a configured, FCK-bound authenticator action. | Per tab; final tab gone → erase live FCK, F only. | SharedWorker/Web Locks may coordinate but do not prove awake-tab liveness; caused write reaches asker, else admitted face session, else waits `seal-awaits-session` (ruling a′). W3C Web Locks describes coordination, not app authority ([[MDN|https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Web_Locks_API]], accessed 2026-10-19). | Unlock A only; direct open/replace/restore/rotate B using all A and F bytes: fail, B ciphertext unchanged; A replacement succeeds. |
| ''iOS phone leaf'' (`device-capabilities-2026.mem:137`) | Same D/F, S=∅. Face secret or a configured authenticator gesture cryptographically bound to FCK unwrap. | Per tab; process eviction/relaunch starts at F and asks again. | No SharedWorker lifetime guarantee in house matrix; Safari background extensions are nonpersistent; never use their presence as a key lease ([[Apple Developer|https://developer.apple.com/documentation/safariservices/optimizing-your-web-extension-for-safari?changes=_5]], 2026-10-19). | Suspend/kill the asker while a seal is pending; only asker result or named wait allowed; relaunch asks again, B remains cryptographically closed. |
