| ''Tablet leaf / proposed waking-floor carrier'' (`device-capabilities-2026.mem:139`; `waking-floor.mem:148,200-202`) | D on mounted faces, F public/ciphertext carriage, S=∅. | Face tabs per-tab unlock; unattended floor sync cannot decrypt D. At final session only F/ciphertext remains. | ''Break:'' any requirement to decrypt/transform private D while unattended conflicts with no-key floor. Ruling: route it to an always-on node, or explicitly add narrowly specified S and boot authorization. Background sync must not silently gain FCK. One tablet probe is bounded to one device (`device-capabilities-2026.mem:200-206`). | Mutate remote private D while tablet is unattended: it may carry ciphertext/F, cannot decrypt or commit a D transformation; after face unlock, that face can sync. |
| ''Installed PWA / iOS Home Screen web app / Android WebAPK'' (`device-capabilities-2026.mem:137-139`) | D/F; S=∅. Install grants no secret. | Per app tab/session; close/relaunch/eviction → F. | Installation affects capability/lifecycle, not row ownership. On iOS it changes web-app mode/push; on Android WebAPK can be a full vessel per house matrix. | Terminate/reinstall/clear volatile state; no D opens before per-face unlock, public F remains readable. |
| ''Probe, e.g. Mudlet'' (`device-capabilities-2026.mem:133,142`) | Target seat owns D/F; probe holds no FCK or S. Reconnect token, if used, is a session credential, not row key. | Each node session presents authority at node; closing probe drops its session, node floor remains. | Outbound-only probe is not a LarVessel; it cannot turn node gate into local custody. | With A session only, ask node for B row; node refuses and probe cannot decrypt bytes locally. |
