The type list below combines canon's one LarVessel/four-host/no-subclass rule (`bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/lar-vessel.mem:20,34`), device-seat matrix (`bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/device-capabilities-2026.mem:129-143`), node classes, and the named planned surfaces. For each, “rows” means the shared census above, filtered to rows that surface can actually hold. `S = ∅` refers to an additional shared *custody payload* after the named place signing seed; current VK wrapping of mixed node rows is not endorsed as target placement. The place signing seed is an extant, separate node S exception detailed below.

| Vessel / seat | Common rows and D/F/S | Any target S; unlock / floor transition | Break or required seam | Single red test |
| ''Node daemon, Lararium/full node'' | Can host all node rows in the prior census: face roots, archives, roster/maps, joins, dyads, handle-book, recovery and outbox-related records → ''D'' by PersonaGroup; public vessel card/charter/floor route data → ''F''; serving rows → ''S only if actually instantiated''. Current hot/cold carrier table: `vault-carriers.ts:287-398`; each boot starts with empty custody holder: `main.ts:336-345,371-374`. | ''Conditional S:'' extant nonempty serving payload only (none measured in current table: `vault-carriers.ts:12-14`). Operator uses face route at `lares vault unlock` once per boot if the target node S class exists; process lock/restart zero-fills keys and composes floor (`custody-holder.ts:18-27,151-155`; `main.ts:462-469`). | Today the single VK is ancestor to mixed rows. Must partition by face and define an SK owner/route before implementing S. Daemon outputs and receipt/log surfaces must not leak typed credentials (`custody-frames.ts:6-23,37`). | With only face A unlocked, direct carrier open/replace/restore/rotation of B must fail and preserve B bytes; floor and public service still boot with no VK; if S rows exist, VK unlock opens only those node rows and no B row. |
| ''Hearth composition'' | Same node store/census as full node; hearth is a lift over the floor, not a new vessel type. Face rows D, public foundation/gate rows F, serving rows conditional S. `main.ts:353-374`; canon `vessel-caps.mem:139-143`. | Same conditional node S; once-per-boot node door; shutdown/lock returns to floor. | A face-bearing hearth needs face admission after node custody unlock; do not treat “node unlocked” as opening every PersonaGroup. Existing implementation binds composition to VK, so target face separation remains work. | Unlock A and mount hearth: read/write A succeeds; B direct row access and B Keyhive/archive appearance fail; lock returns hearth to public floor without losing public serving. |
| ''Herm / crossroads node'' | Place signing seed = ''S'' (private node-only identity, auto-loaded at boot); public verifying key/inception/card/charter and public crossroads/read-face/CAS bytes = ''F''; no held PersonaGroup means no face rows to hold. Future recognized operator data must be D under that operator, never retained as Herm face rows. No serving S row currently: `vault-carriers.ts:12-14`. | Place S auto-opens by process boot today, no human prompt (`node-vessel-identity.ts:429-442`; `open-node-vessel.ts:3283`). There is no current SK/serving-row unlock. Raise uses a recognized operator's own authority and ends at causal boundary/reboot (`main.ts:558-575,604-614`). | Herm cannot seat a face (`personaSlotCeiling` fixed 0). Place S is a measured exception to “floor all public.” Future herm serving rows would add separate S; do not substitute place key for SK. | Boot Herm with zero faces: place signing/read/public carriage works; assert no VK or SK prompt/data opens, no face row is written, and place seed never appears in public output. Reboot preserves only place identity and public floor, not raised caps or face keys. |
| ''CLI seat opening a node session'' | CLI is not a separate LarVessel; it addresses node-owned rows through the socket. Face-scoped commands/backup/recovery are ''D'' to addressed face; public commands are ''F''; CLI holds no vessel S. `packages/lares-cli/src/sealed-act-door.ts:1-21`; `custody-door.ts:2-26`; node frames `custody-frames.ts:135-202`. | ''S = ∅ at CLI.'' Human types node credential only for node unlock (one per boot); each CLI invocation proves its own face/session at gate, no repeat custody prompt. The terminal does not keep keys after the node's lock/shutdown. Roadmap explicitly says each CLI run proves face: `stable-founding-road.mem:201`. | An offline CLI cannot use node-held row keys unless it explicitly receives face recovery material; it must not cache VK or turn successful prior command into implicit cross-face session. | Unlock node as A; invoke CLI under A and then forge/omit/swap face binding for B. A works; every B operation refuses; inspect CLI receipt/daemon outputs for credential bytes and key material—any appearance fails. |
| ''MCP seat / watcher'' | Session seat over CLI/node; same D face rows, F public floor, no MCP-local S. Roadmap classifies MCP and watcher with CLI: own face proof per run (`stable-founding-road.mem:201`). MCP wiring is seat configuration, not authority: `packages/lares-cli/src/codex-wire.ts:70-93`; `vscode-wire.ts:84-150`. | ''S = ∅ at MCP.'' Node unlock remains once/boot; MCP process presents its own face/session on each invocation. Process end does not change node boot state; node lock/restart drops keys. | Long-lived MCP transport can outlive a UI tab; it must re-prove face per session/operation rather than inherit whichever face last used the node. | Keep node unlocked as A; send MCP call claiming B without B admission: it must refuse. Restart MCP and retry: no authority carried. B unlocked separately succeeds only for B. |
| ''Docker/container vessel (harbor, civic, mesh-scenarios)'' | Container's persistent `/state` may carry the same node census; `/workspace` holds bags/wikis. Face rows D, public rows F, optional instantiated serving rows S. Roadmap fixes state mount and host CLI boundary: `stable-founding-road.mem:68,104-109`; restart/unlock flow: `founding-runbook.mem:156`. | ''Conditional S'' exactly same as node; no new container S. Container starts at floor; an attached terminal types unlock after each restart; with no attached human it remains locked/floor. `lararium-container-boot.sh:41-66,110`. Shutdown drops in-memory keys. | Orchestrator restart with no human must not auto-inject a credential or silently unlock. Unattended restart can preserve public floor service, but face/serving capabilities pause until node unlock. This is a deliberate availability boundary. | Kill/restart under unattended orchestration with a surviving state mount: public floor starts; every D and S read refuses until an explicit authorized unlock; no env, image layer, log, or health route contains the unlock credential. |
| ''Node daemon inside harbor / civic / mesh-scenarios'' | Same node D/F/S; place signing seed remains S; container packaging changes lifecycle, not row ownership. `stable-founding-road.mem:56,68,104-109`; seed read `node-vessel-identity.ts:429-442`. | Place S auto-opens each process boot today; any future VK-protected S needs explicit once-per-boot custody door. Container restart returns face/serving keys to floor, but current clear-at-rest place seed remains. | Distinguish daemon restart from CLI/MCP client restart. Orchestrator must not auto-unlock face or serving S without human. | Unattended restart restores place identity/public floor but no face/SK custody; every face/serving operation refuses until authorized node unlock. |

