The per-row RED tests in the tables are the single red witnesses for each type. The shared cryptographic witness must additionally show A's FCK/slot tree cannot open, overwrite, restore, rotate, or derive B's rows even when routing is bypassed; occupied-row replacement authenticates the previous ciphertext before rename (`packages/lararium-browser/src/sealed-writer.ts:208-218,279-309`, already measured in `../PRIOR-YIN.md`). For node, add process-restart and unattended-container restart: fresh boot has no admitted face keys; floor serves only F rows; a named S opens only with node's explicit boot door; no common key opens any face row. This proves the locked D/F/S partition instead of merely proving the router behaved.

