| Browser common acts establish no browser-wide secret. | ''CONFIRM as LEAD.'' The merged census resolves confidential face material to D and intentionally public transport/bootstrap to F; no measured browser S remains. | confirmed-by-both |
| Herm private serving key is the one candidate S. | ''REFINE/REFUTE as a current Herm S.'' `vault-carriers.ts:12-14,249-251` says no serving row exists; `open-node-vessel.ts:558-614` raises with operator caps and has no SK caller. The serving key is a future conditional S, not current. | yours-alone |
| Herm's place signing seed is just public floor material. | ''REFUTE.'' `node-vessel-identity.ts:429-487` reads private seed bytes and uses them to sign; only the public half/card is F. The private seed is a current node-local S-like authority loaded automatically at boot, distinct from VK/SK and face roots. | yours-alone |
| Herm cannot serve before a face exists, because `personaSlotCeiling("herm") === 0`. | ''REFUTE if “serve” means its public/read/relay floor.'' It cannot seat a PersonaGroup, but boots a public read-face/relay and can raise recognized operator caps: `vessel-standing.ts:60-79,113-119`; `open-node-vessel.ts:3242-3291,558-614`. Floor service works without a face or VK. | yours-alone |
| Tablet may do unattended private D sync at floor. | ''REFUTE under the locked law.'' Tablet can carry public/ciphertext sync unattended, but if it must decrypt/transform face rows it needs an authorized face session; otherwise that requirement is an explicit future system S exception. `device-capabilities-2026.mem:139,121`; waking-floor model `waking-floor.mem:148,200`. | confirmed-by-both on boundary; twin-alone on direct device cite |
| Container restart may silently restore face/SK unlock for availability. | ''REFUTE as target.'' Restart drops volatile custody and leaves F; without an explicit human boot authorization, any D or future S is locked. Container wiring is deployment, not authority. `main.ts:336-345,427-430`; `founding-runbook.mem:156`; container entrypoint cited in MINE. | yours-alone |
| CLI and MCP inherit whichever node face last unlocked. | ''REFUTE.'' CLI is a seat against node's socket and must provide act/session authority; roadmap says each CLI run proves face. `sealed-act-door.ts:1-21`, `custody-door.ts:13-30`, `stable-founding-road.mem:201`; MCP wire only configures a session (`codex-wire.ts:70-93`). | yours-alone |
