<<~ ahu slot=`#/r4-yang-yin-lens-applied-to-node-types-additions-and-corrections`>>

!!! YIN lens applied to node types: additions and corrections


''MEASURED:'' The node-wide custody tree currently wraps VK to SK, then keeps both in process memory (`custody-session.ts:80-116,154-190,227-242`; `custody-holder.ts:151-155`). Carrier classification is implementation, not target necessity. There are no serving rows today (`vault-carriers.ts:12-14`). The exception TWIN did not see is the independently loaded place signing seed. It cannot be called F because it is a private signing capability; it also cannot be collapsed into the future serving key. The house must decide whether to protect this key behind a narrow node boot custody door or accept a documented clear-at-rest S exception. The current code auto-opens it on each daemon boot, without a human gesture. This means the strict candidate law “all floor material is public” needs exactly one present-day bend; “floor holds no VK” remains intact.

''LEAD:'' A Herm's zero face ceiling forbids a seated identity, not public operation. The Herm stands before any face and must carry its own place identity. A future Herm serving row could create another S class, but the current serving key has no row to protect. If future system work decrypts a face row while face-less, that breaks D ownership and requires an explicit operator ruling; it cannot silently be charged to SK.

For every node/container/seat type in the previous table, common acts filter as follows (''MEASURED current carriers; LEAD target rows''): founding place signing seed is S on node (public verifying half/card/charter F); PersonaGroup root, FCK and slot tree D; fleet public signed offer/answer F while target-face pending secret/address/join record D; face slot changes/recovery D; private roster, labels, handle-book/recognition graph D while minimal public opaque routes F only after leakage review; Keyhive/Veil archives, dyads, proof/member/Nexus keys D; per-face backup/restore D; clear-custody removes only that face's D and leaves F; future serving rows S only when instantiated and named. The carrier/caller evidence appears in `../PRIOR-YIN.md` and `../PRIOR-YANG.md` census tables and `packages/lararium-node/src/vault-carriers.ts:287-398`; archive row selector remains unresolved.

<<~/ahu>>

