Canon defines ''one LarVessel class, four host families, no subclass'' (`bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/lar-vessel.mem:20-37`); device-seat canon names full vessel, leaf, herm, probe, Android/iOS phones, waking-floor tablet, desktop browser, installed PWA/WebAPK, Mudlet probe, Unreal guest, and planned host/guest surfaces (`bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/device-capabilities-2026.mem:129-143,192`). The following are ''LEAD target'' classifications except where noted. All face-bearing rows in the census are D per PersonaGroup; floor rows are F and hold no VK; browser/leaf/guest S is empty absent a newly named system payload.

| Vessel type | Common row set / S set; face unlock; floor and last-session transition | Bend and single red test |
| Desktop browser tab / browser LarVessel | All private identity, join, archive, roster, dyad, handle, recovery and slots D; public bootstrap/transport F; ''S=∅''. Each tab asks for its own face unlock. Last tab erases live FCK and rests at floor. | Worker lifetime cannot establish an awake-tab roster. Freeze/close asker during seal: route only to its admitted session or same-face admitted unlocked tab, else wait `seal-awaits-session`; no timeout substitution. B direct open/replace fails byte-preserving. |
| iOS phone leaf / Home Screen web app | Same D/F; ''S=∅''; each tab asks independently; app/process loss returns to F and asks again. Installed mode grants no new authority. | No SharedWorker lifetime guarantee in house matrix (`device-capabilities-2026.mem:137`). Red: terminate/suspend tab during asker write; it waits or same-face fallback, never opens sibling row. |
| Android phone leaf | Same D/F; ''S=∅''; per-tab ask; worker/process death returns to floor. | SharedWorker availability is optimization only (`device-capabilities-2026.mem:138`). Red: kill worker while A open; A must re-unlock, B remains cryptographically closed. |
| Tablet waking-floor carrier | Face rows D; public/ciphertext sync F; ''S=∅''; a foreground face session unlocks per tab; last tab leaves floor. | Unattended sync may carry ciphertext/public rows, cannot decrypt or commit D. Red: while unattended, allow F sync and assert D read/modify fails; admit face, then D sync works. |
| Installed PWA / iOS home-screen web app / Android WebAPK | Same D/F; ''S=∅''; each face session unlock; app exit/relaunch returns to F. | Install or OS keychain cannot create a common secret. Red: kill/relaunch and verify no D opens before that face unlock; F stays readable. |
| Probe (Mudlet or other outbound seat) | Probe holds no face custody S and no FCK; addressed node rows remain D/F there; ''S=∅ at probe''. It presents a face/session to node for each call. | Red: with A admitted, ask probe for B row; node refuses, no key material is cached in probe. |
| Native/desktop shell (planned) | D/F; ''S=∅'' unless explicitly reclassified as node herm; app window/session asks for face; final session clears live FCK to F. | OS keychain/biometric may authorize a face FCK unwrap but doesn't alter row ownership. Red: second OS account/session cannot open A/B ciphertext without that face's slot tree. |
| Host ↔ lararium / Unreal guest island (planned) | Host public bridge frames F; face-authorized payload D; guest ''S=∅'' unless it owns a separate key store, in which case independent D/F and own FCK. Guest call presents host-admitted face; end drops guest capability. | If the guest owns keys, model it as a separate vessel; never inherit host VK/FCK. Red: hostile guest reads sibling host row and guest row without its own route; both fail. Exact `#/shore-law` storage contract remains open. |
| Node daemon / full Lararium | D all PersonaGroup records; F public place card/charter/routing; S includes current private place signing seed plus only future named serving payloads. Face sessions present per act; node custody door, if retained for other S, opens once per boot. Restart/shutdown clears volatile VK/SK/FCK; current persistent place seed auto-loads next boot. | Red: one-face node unlock cannot open sibling carriers; fresh restart has no face/serving keys; public floor works and only narrowly named place identity survives. |
| Hearth composition | Same rows as node; place identity S; face D; public shelf F; future serving S conditional. Face admission remains independent after any node boot unlock; lock tears down sovereign composition to floor. | Red: unlock A; A works, B fails cryptographically; lock returns to public floor while preserving public service. |
| Herm / crossroads node | No PersonaGroup rows (ceiling zero); private place seed S; public verifying key/card/crossroads/read/relay F; future serving S only if instantiated; current SK has no consumer. Boot opens place seed automatically, no person prompt; recognized raise uses operator's own caps only for visit; reboot drops raise. | Must serve publicly before any face and cannot store a face. Red: zero-face boot serves public floor, no VK/SK unlock or face rows; private seed never appears in output; reboot drops raised caps but keeps place identity. |
| CLI seat | No local S; node rows addressed by CLI are D by owning face, public operations F. Node unlock once/boot if needed; each CLI run presents own face proof/session. Process exit holds no node keys. | Red: A CLI act passes; missing/forged B binding refuses; receipts/logs contain no credentials or key bytes. |
| MCP / watcher seat | No local S; same node D/F; each invocation/session presents face proof; MCP restart carries no authority; node boot state persists until node lock/restart. | Red: node unlocked under A, MCP call claims B without B admission and refuses; restart MCP does not change that; separate B admission allows only B. |
| Docker/container vessel: harbor, civic, mesh-scenarios | Persistent state may contain node rows: D by face, public F, same node S set (private place seed + only instantiated serving rows); no container-specific S. Start/restart has no face/SK keys; attached operator unlocks node once/boot; absent operator stays floor. | Orchestrator restart cannot auto-inject credentials. Red: restart unattended with persistent volume: public floor comes up; all D/future S refuses; inspect env/image/log/health outputs for no credential. |
| Worker host / generic LarVessel | Same D/F/S according to actual host function; worker role grants no authority. Each face context unlocks only its own FCK; worker/session end drops volatile key; floor F remains. | Red: worker supplied A key context requests B bytes; cryptographic refusal independent of route. |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/r4-yang-roadmap-lock-and-required-house-rulings`>>

!!! Roadmap lock and required house rulings


''MEASURED:'' K15 assigns one identity/store/registry/archive/content-key seat per PersonaGroup; step 6 migrates identity bytes, split stores, archive format together (`bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:203,456`; `keyhive-per-persona-group-2026.mem:55-72`). F6 slice three consumes face context for asker-sealed writes (`stable-founding-road.mem:504`). The road map calls for per-run CLI face proof (`:201`); the previously merged handbacks identify B1 as browser/no-VK target (`../PRIOR-YIN.md`, `../PRIOR-YANG.md`).

''LEAD sequencing:'' K15.1 defines exhaustive D/F/S row schema and independent FCK + own slot/recovery tree; K15.1/.2 puts identity, archives and mixed carrier splits under each PersonaGroup with no identity above them; K15.3 plus F6 slice three binds each tab/session to one face and enforces (a′), including safe open-before-replace; K15.4 clears one face's rows/route without sibling rotation; K15.5 restores one face alone; K15.6 migrates identity bytes, split stores, FCK slots and archives under one migration fence. B1 lands browser D/F, no VK, per-tab asks and final-tab floor. Node/CLI/MCP consume the same D/F ownership, while node boot custody applies only to an explicitly retained S. The Herm serving-key row remains conditional and empty today. Containers honor node cadence but never unlock unattended. The place signing seed requires a separate operator ruling because it is already a private boot-loaded key: narrow boot protection or documented clear-at-rest exception. Tablet unattended private transformation and guest-owned key store also require explicit ruling if demanded.

