!!! Trade (a): audit of TWIN's top claims


| TWIN claim | Trade verdict and source check (2026-10-19) | Provenance |
| Place seed rests as clear hex JSON, mode 0600, in identity directory; boot loader validates key and inception. | ''CONFIRM.'' `node-vessel-identity.ts:140-170,185-198,429-448`; startup load at `open-node-vessel.ts:945-946`. 0600 limits other local users; it is not encryption or host/root protection. | twin-alone |
| Identity is separate from custody VK/SK and is listed at floor; Herm receives it. | ''CONFIRM.'' `vault-carriers.ts:239-251`; `open-node-vessel.ts:3283`. This is a private place key at floor, so the earlier literal “no vessel key” law conflicts with code; no-custody-key is accurate. | confirmed-by-both |
| Place KEL has only self-signed inception, no next-key commitment or rotation/recovery path. | ''CONFIRM.'' `vessel-kel.ts:2-13,35-59`; `node-vessel-identity.ts:185-198`; TWIN's source search found only inception/decode/verify. `nexus seal rotate` and VK rotation are different key/authority lanes. Current recovery is abandon/re-found and update dependent pins/relationships (the operational steps are LEAD). | twin-alone |
| Seed consumer inventory includes carry-for contracts/floor pins, asks, device/group-secret operations, relay gate derivation, carriage, CLI/founding, dyad founder veil derivation, and floor card. | ''CONFIRM, with scope caveat.'' Opened cited sites: `commands/nexus-contract.ts:250-268`; `open-node-vessel.ts:1217,1394,1450,2150,2279-2280,3087,3103,3115`; `commands/fleet-join.ts:285+`; `commands/init.ts:246-251,320-327,491-510`; `lares-cli/src/commands/meme.ts:1117`; `lararium-mesh/src/dyad.ts:399-402`; `main.ts:765-769`. TWIN's inventory is substantially more complete than the initial YIN handoff. Exact data reachable through the group-secret opener still requires separate record-level audit. | twin-alone |
| Floor-gate child derivation uses a narrow registered-domain door and clears its local seed buffer. | ''CONFIRM.'' `node-vessel-identity.ts:454-499`; `hearth-sovereign-pin.ts:56`; `herm-carriage.ts:64`. A stolen root seed can still reproduce registered derivations; caller API restriction is not protection after seed theft. | twin-alone |
| Public card is cached material rather than freshly signed at each boot. | ''CONFIRM.'' `node-vessel-identity.ts:359-393`; card file mode at `:359-372`. Seed participation in Keyhive founding does not make the cached card a secret. | twin-alone |
| KEL signatures or current code detect a thief's valid signatures / rotate to recover. | ''REFUTE if implied.'' Current KEL has no succession record: valid attacker signatures under the stolen key are indistinguishable to a verifier that only has the existing key. Kapae/re-found are not an automatic revoke protocol. Independent witnesses might detect conflicting histories only if a transparency/consistency mechanism is built and relied on; that is proposed, not measured. | yours-alone |
| Herm can publish/serve floor without a human; founding, fleet join, and carry-for can wait for an operator. | ''CONFIRM.'' Seed loads at boot and floor door is usable while locked (`open-node-vessel.ts:945-946`; `node-vessel-identity.ts:454-470`). Explicit CLI paths cited above are operator commands. Exact products that need to be available on an asleep/waking floor remain deployment/product decisions. | confirmed-by-both |
